## 2. Prepare the project and file locations

Start with an existing React Native app that runs locally and a selected Bitrise template with the required Sauce Labs integration. The supplied v1.10.0 build sample omits Sauce Labs. Have the owner confirm the approved version for your application.

| Prerequisite | What to confirm before copying |
|---|---|
| React Native | Existing app entry point, approved dependencies, and a safe demo destination. |
| Jest component testing | Existing Jest/Babel setup and an approved compatible `@testing-library/react-native` version. Preserve the React Native preset and existing setup. |
| Appium JavaScript | Actual runner and framework. This example uses a compatible pinned WebdriverIO CLI, local runner, Mocha framework, globals, spec reporter, and Sauce service in the shared tooling. |
| Native suites | Use the native tabs only with configured AndroidJUnitRunner/Espresso dependencies or an Xcode UI-test target. |
| Sauce Labs | Approved account, region, exact uploaded app reference, device/OS, and test-run permissions. |

